'' ONE QUOTED STRING AND NO MORE. fbc's answer to '#cmdline "-d A" "-d B"' is its
'' error 3 at the second string ("Expected End-of-Line, found '-d B'"), so the two
'' are not quietly concatenated into one command line and are not silently half-read.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --parse-only %s
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: TKO0333
'' EXPECT-OUT: #cmdline takes one quoted argument string

#cmdline "-d A" "-d B"
print "x"
